# vlc-bittorrent v@VERSION@ for official VLC @VLC_VERSION@ (win32 / x86)

Built from commit: @COMMIT_SHA@
Built on: @BUILD_DATE@
Build job: @BUILD_JOB_URL@

## Files

- `libaccess_bittorrent_plugin.dll` (5-6 MB, stripped)

## Install

1. Copy `libaccess_bittorrent_plugin.dll` into:
   ```
   C:\Program Files (x86)\VideoLAN\VLC\plugins\access\
   ```
2. Delete VLC's plugin cache so it re-scans for the new plugin:
   ```
   %APPDATA%\vlc\plugins-*.dat
   ```
   (typically `C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Roaming\vlc\plugins-*.dat`)
3. Start VLC and open a `.torrent` file or a magnet link:
   ```
   vlc video.torrent
   vlc "magnet:?xt=urn:btih:..."
   ```

## Verifying it loaded

After launching VLC with a torrent, the message log
(`Tools` → `Messages`, verbosity 2) should contain lines like:

```
bittorrent: Bittorrent metadata access
bittorrent: Bittorrent data access
bittorrent: Bittorrent magnet metadata access
```

## Verified ABI compatibility

- PE32 Intel i386 (32-bit, matches official win32 build)
- Exports `vlc_entry__3_0_0f` (matches official plugin ABI)
- Links `msvcrt.dll` + `libvlccore.dll` (no ucrt, no libgcc/libstdc++ DLLs)
- Statically linked libgcc/libstdc++/libwinpthread — no extra runtime DLLs needed

## Known limitations

- **libtorrent encryption is disabled** (no OpenSSL linked); private trackers
  that mandate protocol encryption will not connect. Public BitTorrent swarms
  work normally.
- libtorrent's HTTPS tracker support is unavailable (would require
  OpenSSL/GnuTLS). HTTP and UDP trackers work.
- **32-bit only**; will not load in a 64-bit VLC build. Use the official
  `vlc-@VLC_VERSION@-win32.exe` / `.zip` / `.msi`.
